[[:db/retract 17592186120471 :question/answer-fields 17592186118940] [:db/retract 17592186198716 :question/answer-fields 17592186194922] {:db/id 17592186083226 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-eb3ce7a3-f936-5690-b0b8-a114f6f8251b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-eb3ce7a3-f936-5690-b0b8-a114f6f8251b" :question/id #uuid "eb3ce7a3-f936-5690-b0b8-a114f6f8251b" :question/math-academy-id "q-94453" :question/problem "A data set has mean $\\overset{―}{x}=17$ and variance ${\\sigma }^{2}=4.06.$ Find the $z$-score of an observation $x=12.3,$ giving your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "The $z$-score of an observation $x$ is defined by\n\n$$\nz=\\frac{x-\\overset{―}{x}}{\\sigma }.\n$$\n\nThe $z$-score represents how many standard deviations an observation is above or below the data set's mean.\n\nHere, we're told that the mean is $\\overset{―}{x}=17,$ and we can calculate the standard deviation as\n\n$$\n\\sigma =\\sqrt{{\\sigma }^{2}}=\\sqrt{4.06}.\n$$\n\nSo, the $z$-score of the observation $x=12.3$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =\\frac{x-\\overset{―}{x}}{\\sigma } \\\\  & ≈\\frac{12.3-17}{\\sqrt{4.06}} \\\\  & ≈-2.33\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nto $2$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c3ced3f9-cf87-5626-9fe8-981ef8efa9ee"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c3ced3f9-cf87-5626-9fe8-981ef8efa9ee" :answer-field/id #uuid "c3ced3f9-cf87-5626-9fe8-981ef8efa9ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-93d69dcc-fcf9-5ce1-b378-436d89621a08" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f8448585-d93f-51b6-bc8a-68dec4e10458" "answer-a033f62b-8ca0-5377-b0c9-fe5ba766a0a9" "answer-93d69dcc-fcf9-5ce1-b378-436d89621a08" "answer-0f31a88c-1ba4-598e-907c-0f9606b6bc76" "answer-238400b2-7007-51fd-962d-7ef0d78021e8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f8448585-d93f-51b6-bc8a-68dec4e10458" :answer/id #uuid "f8448585-d93f-51b6-bc8a-68dec4e10458" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1.45" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a033f62b-8ca0-5377-b0c9-fe5ba766a0a9" :answer/id #uuid "a033f62b-8ca0-5377-b0c9-fe5ba766a0a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1.92" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-93d69dcc-fcf9-5ce1-b378-436d89621a08" :answer/id #uuid "93d69dcc-fcf9-5ce1-b378-436d89621a08" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2.33" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0f31a88c-1ba4-598e-907c-0f9606b6bc76" :answer/id #uuid "0f31a88c-1ba4-598e-907c-0f9606b6bc76" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.78" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-238400b2-7007-51fd-962d-7ef0d78021e8" :answer/id #uuid "238400b2-7007-51fd-962d-7ef0d78021e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054719 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-56f00061-e4f7-5bf8-94e9-0bb7b8e48e5a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-56f00061-e4f7-5bf8-94e9-0bb7b8e48e5a" :question/id #uuid "56f00061-e4f7-5bf8-94e9-0bb7b8e48e5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-64985" :question/problem "![](images/0b/0beb8842ac4b8781a90973a5f56d4c8b5fc27f42af549fe23a9f9042b3067c9b.png)\n\nThe point $P(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3},\\frac{2}{3})$ lies on the unit circle, as shown. What is $\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta ?$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/78/7895e1fbe54cd3dea65ba1c75d79c6f325f14cd6bc55f9c7ad99299f00b516df.png)\n\nAny point $(x,y)$ on the unit circle is related to the central angle $\\theta $ as follows:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nWe're given that $x=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}$ and $y=\\frac{2}{3}$ at the point $P.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$\n\nKnowing that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta },$ we can calculate $\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta =\\frac{(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3})}{(\\frac{2}{3})}=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-68de66ac-80f1-54a7-9937-cf3796a8eb5c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-68de66ac-80f1-54a7-9937-cf3796a8eb5c" :answer-field/id #uuid "68de66ac-80f1-54a7-9937-cf3796a8eb5c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c0b882d3-6685-54b3-9143-be0ca09e65f1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8cbd082b-7271-584a-97ee-c98f1ef18db8" "answer-52272410-c3a7-5f3d-9aa2-2bb605056bc5" "answer-1fe31d62-2abc-5e23-8ff1-a5691122e568" "answer-c0b882d3-6685-54b3-9143-be0ca09e65f1" "answer-2be78953-a839-5dd5-9851-a03182d65086"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8cbd082b-7271-584a-97ee-c98f1ef18db8" :answer/id #uuid "8cbd082b-7271-584a-97ee-c98f1ef18db8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-52272410-c3a7-5f3d-9aa2-2bb605056bc5" :answer/id #uuid "52272410-c3a7-5f3d-9aa2-2bb605056bc5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1fe31d62-2abc-5e23-8ff1-a5691122e568" :answer/id #uuid "1fe31d62-2abc-5e23-8ff1-a5691122e568" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c0b882d3-6685-54b3-9143-be0ca09e65f1" :answer/id #uuid "c0b882d3-6685-54b3-9143-be0ca09e65f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2be78953-a839-5dd5-9851-a03182d65086" :answer/id #uuid "2be78953-a839-5dd5-9851-a03182d65086" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186184140 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-4c03278b-ee04-5a97-ab36-8794ca017e49"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-4c03278b-ee04-5a97-ab36-8794ca017e49" :question/id #uuid "4c03278b-ee04-5a97-ab36-8794ca017e49" :question/math-academy-id "q-64807" :question/problem "What is $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{14\\pi }{5})$ expressed in terms of a reference angle?" :question/worked-solution "We wish to express $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{14\\pi }{5})$ in terms of $\\operatorname{tan}⁡{\\theta }_{R},$ where ${\\theta }_{R}$ is the reference angle corresponding to the angle $\\theta =\\frac{14\\pi }{5}.$\n\nTo express $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{14\\pi }{5})$ in terms of $\\operatorname{tan}⁡{\\theta }_{R},$ we proceed as follows:\n\n- **Step 1**: Find the corresponding coterminal angle that lies in the range $[0,2\\pi ).$ We do this by subtracting integer multiples of $2\\pi $ until we get our desired angle.\n\n$$\n\\frac{14\\pi }{5}-2\\pi =\\frac{4\\pi }{5}\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{14\\pi }{5})=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{4\\pi }{5}).\n$$\n\n![](images/5e/5e1c95cc4e399b1902d230165341daa7388234b5edf7a64503f0007c34785242.png)\n\n- **Step 2**: Compute the reference angle. Since $\\theta =\\frac{4\\pi }{5}$ is in the $2$nd quadrant, the reference angle is\n\n$$\n{\\theta }_{R}=\\pi -\\frac{4\\pi }{5}=\\frac{\\pi }{5}.\n$$\n\n- **Step 3**: Determine the correct sign. The tangent function is negative $(-)$ in the second quadrant. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{14\\pi }{5})=-\\operatorname{tan}⁡{\\theta }_{R}=-\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5}).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{14\\pi }{5})=-\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5}).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f0f034cb-e519-5576-b681-123ffbbc1af7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f0f034cb-e519-5576-b681-123ffbbc1af7" :answer-field/id #uuid "f0f034cb-e519-5576-b681-123ffbbc1af7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a0639da0-5029-579e-bb08-b015ba8a2e7f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1afde537-3e74-5946-b386-3ed83eaae80a" "answer-a0639da0-5029-579e-bb08-b015ba8a2e7f" "answer-45f93d8a-5e35-5d60-bc54-1a699dd082b9" "answer-602f4b55-ce6b-500e-ae5f-aed50fee8755" "answer-5062bbde-f199-52b4-b588-137d165578dc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1afde537-3e74-5946-b386-3ed83eaae80a" :answer/id #uuid "1afde537-3e74-5946-b386-3ed83eaae80a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{10})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a0639da0-5029-579e-bb08-b015ba8a2e7f" :answer/id #uuid "a0639da0-5029-579e-bb08-b015ba8a2e7f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-45f93d8a-5e35-5d60-bc54-1a699dd082b9" :answer/id #uuid "45f93d8a-5e35-5d60-bc54-1a699dd082b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{5})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-602f4b55-ce6b-500e-ae5f-aed50fee8755" :answer/id #uuid "602f4b55-ce6b-500e-ae5f-aed50fee8755" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{10})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5062bbde-f199-52b4-b588-137d165578dc" :answer/id #uuid "5062bbde-f199-52b4-b588-137d165578dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064308 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-29625a08-0232-5ce8-97e1-f2bb9cf1a9d3"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-29625a08-0232-5ce8-97e1-f2bb9cf1a9d3" :question/id #uuid "29625a08-0232-5ce8-97e1-f2bb9cf1a9d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-138856" :question/problem "Consider the function $y=(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{5x}.$ Its derivative is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=5(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{5x}\\cdot g(x).\n$$\n\nFind the function $g(x).$" :question/worked-solution "We have the function \n\n$$\ny=(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{5x}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we take the natural logarithm of both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡((\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{5x}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =5x\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we differentiate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)) \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot {y}^{′} & =(5x)^{′}\\cdot (\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x))+(5x)\\cdot {(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x))}^{′} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot {y}^{′} & =5\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+5x\\cdot (\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)) \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{′}}{y} & =5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-5x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{′}}{y} & =5(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for ${y}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =y(5(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $y=(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{5x}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =5(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{5x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-19581f53-386c-55c5-88ff-b5d2b3116bb1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-19581f53-386c-55c5-88ff-b5d2b3116bb1" :answer-field/id #uuid "19581f53-386c-55c5-88ff-b5d2b3116bb1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-80147df6-2320-55c9-944a-766dbd01c6c9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b4326574-8b69-5df3-9063-abf1241c8efd" "answer-9c2b317b-6389-5a05-8b28-b44cfeff3161" "answer-543a59b8-c1fa-5f13-aee5-fec0cb00f970" "answer-80147df6-2320-55c9-944a-766dbd01c6c9" "answer-11871c64-6368-59c5-9ec4-a19994f69e2e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b4326574-8b69-5df3-9063-abf1241c8efd" :answer/id #uuid "b4326574-8b69-5df3-9063-abf1241c8efd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+5x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9c2b317b-6389-5a05-8b28-b44cfeff3161" :answer/id #uuid "9c2b317b-6389-5a05-8b28-b44cfeff3161" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-543a59b8-c1fa-5f13-aee5-fec0cb00f970" :answer/id #uuid "543a59b8-c1fa-5f13-aee5-fec0cb00f970" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-80147df6-2320-55c9-944a-766dbd01c6c9" :answer/id #uuid "80147df6-2320-55c9-944a-766dbd01c6c9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-11871c64-6368-59c5-9ec4-a19994f69e2e" :answer/id #uuid "11871c64-6368-59c5-9ec4-a19994f69e2e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-x{tan}^{2}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186329947 :question/problem "If a curve $C$ is given by $y=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,$ calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x=e.$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate using the product rule. Let $u(x)=x$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}.\n$$\n\nApplying the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}+(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we now substitute $x=e$ into the formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=e} & =1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x \\\\  & =1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡e \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line is $2.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186208845 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-4a25c2e7-c512-5e51-abef-9e2f7de41d8d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-4a25c2e7-c512-5e51-abef-9e2f7de41d8d" :question/id #uuid "4a25c2e7-c512-5e51-abef-9e2f7de41d8d" :question/math-academy-id "q-350398" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nGiven the matrices above, write $A{x}^{T}⊙(y+{x}^{T})$ as a matrix product.\n\n| $A{x}^{T}⊙(y+{x}^{T})=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |  |  | {{field-3}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $0$ | $5$ |  |  |  | $4$ |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "The Hadamard product of two compatible vectors $u$ and $v$ can be expressed as the matrix product\n\n$$\nv⊙u=\\text{diag}(v)u.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nA{x}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}14 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\ny+{x}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that they are of the same size; hence, their Hadamard product is well-defined. We conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{x}^{T}⊙(y+{x}^{T}) & =\\text{diag}(A{x}^{T})(y+{x}^{T}) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}14 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b260ade0-56c3-56dd-a4a0-d5986f71deaa" "answer-field-41ca39fc-2d4b-570d-9f24-83e1c58f7ccd" "answer-field-dfe6a128-451b-5111-8b37-193d93e921e1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b260ade0-56c3-56dd-a4a0-d5986f71deaa" :answer-field/id #uuid "b260ade0-56c3-56dd-a4a0-d5986f71deaa" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-d39b5577-1d88-52f5-8392-fa15da6032a1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d39b5577-1d88-52f5-8392-fa15da6032a1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d39b5577-1d88-52f5-8392-fa15da6032a1" :answer/id #uuid "d39b5577-1d88-52f5-8392-fa15da6032a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-41ca39fc-2d4b-570d-9f24-83e1c58f7ccd" :answer-field/id #uuid "41ca39fc-2d4b-570d-9f24-83e1c58f7ccd" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-2896ca3f-d858-5e74-86f4-6d0d60e64ff9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2896ca3f-d858-5e74-86f4-6d0d60e64ff9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2896ca3f-d858-5e74-86f4-6d0d60e64ff9" :answer/id #uuid "2896ca3f-d858-5e74-86f4-6d0d60e64ff9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dfe6a128-451b-5111-8b37-193d93e921e1" :answer-field/id #uuid "dfe6a128-451b-5111-8b37-193d93e921e1" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-8962625e-b9ec-5993-8137-11eca943599a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8962625e-b9ec-5993-8137-11eca943599a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8962625e-b9ec-5993-8137-11eca943599a" :answer/id #uuid "8962625e-b9ec-5993-8137-11eca943599a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105737 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-35202296-3c02-529f-93c9-ab75d2fe58b2"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-35202296-3c02-529f-93c9-ab75d2fe58b2" :question/id #uuid "35202296-3c02-529f-93c9-ab75d2fe58b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-128355" :question/problem "Find $c\\cdot (a\\times b),$ if $b\\times c=⟨4,3,-5⟩$ and $a=⟨-2,8,2⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the triple scalar product \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨-2,8,2⟩\\cdot ⟨4,3,-5⟩ \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot 4+8\\cdot 3+2\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =-8+24-10 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we swap $a$ and $c$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\cdot (b\\times a)=-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand again we swap $a$ and $b$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\cdot (a\\times b)=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-81bc68bf-9d8f-562a-bde6-27ff85778ca1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-81bc68bf-9d8f-562a-bde6-27ff85778ca1" :answer-field/id #uuid "81bc68bf-9d8f-562a-bde6-27ff85778ca1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6cddf496-550e-503d-97cf-86f4c416cb41" :answer-field/choices ["answer-87da3e47-9864-54d6-b40d-2913c6ae3373" "answer-f7d42b31-2f13-5fd5-a529-f48c87f1b72a" "answer-ba4d127a-493d-5de0-a877-1ac772d55fad" "answer-29595116-806d-5a50-ab1b-9695013bab97" "answer-6cddf496-550e-503d-97cf-86f4c416cb41"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-87da3e47-9864-54d6-b40d-2913c6ae3373" :answer/id #uuid "87da3e47-9864-54d6-b40d-2913c6ae3373" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-22" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f7d42b31-2f13-5fd5-a529-f48c87f1b72a" :answer/id #uuid "f7d42b31-2f13-5fd5-a529-f48c87f1b72a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ba4d127a-493d-5de0-a877-1ac772d55fad" :answer/id #uuid "ba4d127a-493d-5de0-a877-1ac772d55fad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "22" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-29595116-806d-5a50-ab1b-9695013bab97" :answer/id #uuid "29595116-806d-5a50-ab1b-9695013bab97" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "26" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6cddf496-550e-503d-97cf-86f4c416cb41" :answer/id #uuid "6cddf496-550e-503d-97cf-86f4c416cb41" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068786 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-0a661730-d4ec-53a7-9567-e2d3f75e3bd0"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-0a661730-d4ec-53a7-9567-e2d3f75e3bd0" :question/id #uuid "0a661730-d4ec-53a7-9567-e2d3f75e3bd0" :question/math-academy-id "q-113727" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{{x}^{5}}{\\sqrt{2-{x}^{6}}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=2-{x}^{6}.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-6{x}^{5}\\,⟹\\,(-\\frac{1}{6})\\text{d}u={x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nand we can solve the resulting integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{5}}{\\sqrt{2-{x}^{6}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2-{x}^{6}}}\\cdot {x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{6})\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{6}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{6}(2\\sqrt{u})+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt{u}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt{2-{x}^{6}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ba44c6c6-d2e7-5fc3-91bc-e559cd6937b2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ba44c6c6-d2e7-5fc3-91bc-e559cd6937b2" :answer-field/id #uuid "ba44c6c6-d2e7-5fc3-91bc-e559cd6937b2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e721585d-c9aa-5992-9200-4910767201bd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0678af68-2cfb-5844-963f-561512f9006d" "answer-e721585d-c9aa-5992-9200-4910767201bd" "answer-e1c194db-8c56-5f8b-9caf-143ea6db9c78" "answer-327adc54-a9df-5f2d-b704-5f8e97ebeefa" "answer-9fb4fe7b-3555-57fe-b8fa-15be7b061577"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0678af68-2cfb-5844-963f-561512f9006d" :answer/id #uuid "0678af68-2cfb-5844-963f-561512f9006d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2-{x}^{6}}}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e721585d-c9aa-5992-9200-4910767201bd" :answer/id #uuid "e721585d-c9aa-5992-9200-4910767201bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt{2-{x}^{6}}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e1c194db-8c56-5f8b-9caf-143ea6db9c78" :answer/id #uuid "e1c194db-8c56-5f8b-9caf-143ea6db9c78" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6}\\sqrt{2-{x}^{6}}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-327adc54-a9df-5f2d-b704-5f8e97ebeefa" :answer/id #uuid "327adc54-a9df-5f2d-b704-5f8e97ebeefa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}\\sqrt{2-{x}^{6}}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9fb4fe7b-3555-57fe-b8fa-15be7b061577" :answer/id #uuid "9fb4fe7b-3555-57fe-b8fa-15be7b061577" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt{2-{x}^{6}}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166969 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-81c0e5cb-c8d5-5dbe-9be3-3283a12b1fd6"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-81c0e5cb-c8d5-5dbe-9be3-3283a12b1fd6" :question/id #uuid "81c0e5cb-c8d5-5dbe-9be3-3283a12b1fd6" :question/math-academy-id "q-347435" :question/problem "Consider the function\n\n$$\np(x)=1[x\\ge 0]\\cdot {x}^{2}+1[-3\\le x<0]\\cdot 1+1[x<-3]\\cdot (-2x).\n$$\n\nWhat is $p(-5)?$" :question/worked-solution "The indicator function $1[P]$ equals $1$ if the predicate $P$ is true and $0$ if $P$ is false.\n\n$$\n1[P]={\\begin{aligned}1, & \\text{if }P\\text{ is true}, \\\\ 0, & \\text{if }P\\text{ is false}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=-5,$ we evaluate each indicator function:\n\n- $1[x\\ge 0]=1[-5\\ge 0]=0$ (since $-5\\ge 0$ is false)\n\n- $1[-3\\le x<0]=1[-3\\le -5<0]=0$ (since $-3\\le -5$ is false)\n\n- $1[x<-3]=1[-5<-3]=1$ (since $-5<-3$ is true)\n\nSubstituting into the expression for $p(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(-5) & =0\\cdot 25+0\\cdot 1+1\\cdot (-2(-5)) \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that the indicator functions act as a \"switch\": since $x=-5<-3,$ only the third term contributes to the result." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-bc02869c-5264-53f2-a4f6-8cbf93737163"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bc02869c-5264-53f2-a4f6-8cbf93737163" :answer-field/id #uuid "bc02869c-5264-53f2-a4f6-8cbf93737163" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-cc721ea0-7d36-594b-a9cd-3c0139aedbbf" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0e9019fa-53e3-5da4-b1e0-9f5b7131cd05" "answer-f50e6a52-629e-5669-b331-2a7ee1fc70ba" "answer-c5cac1e7-f645-5ed2-9530-e49763a8397e" "answer-cc721ea0-7d36-594b-a9cd-3c0139aedbbf" "answer-7465856e-9a5d-527e-9054-c95c24ffdaef"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0e9019fa-53e3-5da4-b1e0-9f5b7131cd05" :answer/id #uuid "0e9019fa-53e3-5da4-b1e0-9f5b7131cd05" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f50e6a52-629e-5669-b331-2a7ee1fc70ba" :answer/id #uuid "f50e6a52-629e-5669-b331-2a7ee1fc70ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c5cac1e7-f645-5ed2-9530-e49763a8397e" :answer/id #uuid "c5cac1e7-f645-5ed2-9530-e49763a8397e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cc721ea0-7d36-594b-a9cd-3c0139aedbbf" :answer/id #uuid "cc721ea0-7d36-594b-a9cd-3c0139aedbbf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7465856e-9a5d-527e-9054-c95c24ffdaef" :answer/id #uuid "7465856e-9a5d-527e-9054-c95c24ffdaef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162159 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8220b103-348c-5b5b-b0e1-61384fcc7157"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-8220b103-348c-5b5b-b0e1-61384fcc7157" :question/id #uuid "8220b103-348c-5b5b-b0e1-61384fcc7157" :question/math-academy-id "q-253140" :question/problem "![](images/b6/b6abb4332c7601200fec40e8b3f8e6f6f8c81004aaa92af936063625a5c9f2e8.png)\n\nWhat is the infimum of the function $y=f(x)$ shown above?\n\n${inf}_{x\\in R}f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The infimum of a function is the infimum of the range of the function.\n\nIn this case, the range of $f$ is $A=(-3,2).$\n\nTo find the infimum of a set $A,$ we must find the set containing **all** lower bounds of $A$ (i.e., the set of lower bounds) and take the maximum of this set.\n\nSo, in our case, we have that\n\n- any number $y\\le -3$ is a lower bound of $A,$\n\n- any number $y>-3$ is **not** a lower bound of $A.$ In other words, we can always find an element of $A$ that is smaller than $y$ for any $y>-3.$\n\nTherefore, $(-\\infty ,-3]$ is the set of lower bounds of $A,$ and\n\n$$\n{inf}_{x\\in R}f(x)=inf(A)=max(-\\infty ,-3]=-3.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b74cd008-64ba-599d-b9ba-bae5a27661b2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b74cd008-64ba-599d-b9ba-bae5a27661b2" :answer-field/id #uuid "b74cd008-64ba-599d-b9ba-bae5a27661b2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-714d3c80-c42b-53fa-ac34-c002e7d83a01" :answer-field/choices ["answer-714d3c80-c42b-53fa-ac34-c002e7d83a01"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-714d3c80-c42b-53fa-ac34-c002e7d83a01" :answer/id #uuid "714d3c80-c42b-53fa-ac34-c002e7d83a01" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166738 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e1b12ff8-1521-511b-83f5-03f8cbdd4a50"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-e1b12ff8-1521-511b-83f5-03f8cbdd4a50" :question/id #uuid "e1b12ff8-1521-511b-83f5-03f8cbdd4a50" :question/math-academy-id "q-225084" :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(10)$ given below, compute $P(X\\ge 7).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ | $9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0103\\,$ | $\\,0.0293\\,$ | $\\,0.0671\\,$ | $\\,0.1301\\,$ | $\\,0.2202\\,$ | $\\,0.3328\\,$ | $\\,0.4579\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTo solve the given problem, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(X>a)=1-P(X\\le a)=1-F(a).\n$$\n\nNow, note that \n\n$$\nP(X\\ge 7)=P(X>6).\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 7) & =P(X>6) \\\\  & =1-P(X\\le 6) \\\\  & =1-F(6) \\\\  & =1-0.1301 \\\\  & =0.8699.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a3f83418-67ae-557d-89d1-ea574cfdaef1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a3f83418-67ae-557d-89d1-ea574cfdaef1" :answer-field/id #uuid "a3f83418-67ae-557d-89d1-ea574cfdaef1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d9469c50-bd92-5809-9036-77ef3324feb0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-687283b6-5499-5bd2-b076-a93e5e440109" "answer-e40e4629-665c-5952-9423-1e72a8b77087" "answer-145fb916-9aed-5e0c-805d-bdf8e795a910" "answer-38ba9fc1-79f2-5b6b-912c-c6c105703d2d" "answer-d9469c50-bd92-5809-9036-77ef3324feb0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-687283b6-5499-5bd2-b076-a93e5e440109" :answer/id #uuid "687283b6-5499-5bd2-b076-a93e5e440109" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.2202" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e40e4629-665c-5952-9423-1e72a8b77087" :answer/id #uuid "e40e4629-665c-5952-9423-1e72a8b77087" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.3328" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-145fb916-9aed-5e0c-805d-bdf8e795a910" :answer/id #uuid "145fb916-9aed-5e0c-805d-bdf8e795a910" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.6672" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-38ba9fc1-79f2-5b6b-912c-c6c105703d2d" :answer/id #uuid "38ba9fc1-79f2-5b6b-912c-c6c105703d2d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.7798" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d9469c50-bd92-5809-9036-77ef3324feb0" :answer/id #uuid "d9469c50-bd92-5809-9036-77ef3324feb0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.8699" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186233501 :question/worked-solution "First of all, we need to find the slope of the normal line at the point $(1,\\,0).$   Remember that the slope of the normal line, ${m}^{′},$ is the negative reciprocal of the slope of the tangent line:\n\n$$\n{m}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{m}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we will calculate the derivative using implicit differentiation, assuming that $y=y(x).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(xy+{x}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(xy)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y+2x & =0 \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-(2x+y) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{2x+y}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the slope of the tangent at the point $(1,\\,0)$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}_{(1,\\,0)} \\\\  & ={(-\\frac{2x+y}{x})}_{(1,\\,0)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2\\cdot 1+0}{1} \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the normal line is ${m}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{m}=-\\frac{1}{-2}=\\frac{1}{2}.$ We can write the equation of the normal at the point $(1,\\,0)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-{y}_{1}) & ={m}^{′}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ (y-0) & =\\frac{1}{2}(x-1) \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{2}(x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we just need to find where this normal line intersects the $y$-axis. At the point $P$ the $x$-coordinate is $0,$ so we set $x=0$ and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{1}{2}(x-1) \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{2}(0-1) \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of $P$ are $(0,\\,-\\frac{1}{2}).$" :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-40bccfca-586d-50c1-9dd5-02226a8edd85"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-40bccfca-586d-50c1-9dd5-02226a8edd85" :answer-field/id #uuid "40bccfca-586d-50c1-9dd5-02226a8edd85" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f6d5b8d1-56ce-5658-ab8d-6cb521d7bf4e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d3a2a8e4-cff5-5de9-a017-294e1b3e3090" "answer-b71c047d-d0a4-59a9-94d3-e9b03771936d" "answer-f6d5b8d1-56ce-5658-ab8d-6cb521d7bf4e" "answer-cda0515f-1f4d-516f-be38-223dff8af225" "answer-e659e298-eaa5-5dc6-b4eb-0351e4a2b803"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d3a2a8e4-cff5-5de9-a017-294e1b3e3090" :answer/id #uuid "d3a2a8e4-cff5-5de9-a017-294e1b3e3090" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,\\,-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b71c047d-d0a4-59a9-94d3-e9b03771936d" :answer/id #uuid "b71c047d-d0a4-59a9-94d3-e9b03771936d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,\\,-2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f6d5b8d1-56ce-5658-ab8d-6cb521d7bf4e" :answer/id #uuid "f6d5b8d1-56ce-5658-ab8d-6cb521d7bf4e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,\\,-\\frac{1}{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cda0515f-1f4d-516f-be38-223dff8af225" :answer/id #uuid "cda0515f-1f4d-516f-be38-223dff8af225" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,\\,1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e659e298-eaa5-5dc6-b4eb-0351e4a2b803" :answer/id #uuid "e659e298-eaa5-5dc6-b4eb-0351e4a2b803" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,\\,\\frac{1}{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129146 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-22ed86af-8be9-5e5f-bb20-a371a80d9316"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-22ed86af-8be9-5e5f-bb20-a371a80d9316" :question/id #uuid "22ed86af-8be9-5e5f-bb20-a371a80d9316" :question/math-academy-id "q-39252" :question/problem "Given that $(x-2)$ is a factor of $f(x)=-{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-3x+2,$ which of the following curves is generated by $y=f(x)?$\n\n(*Note: Figures not drawn to scale*)" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to factor the polynomial. We are told that $(x-2)$ is a factor of $f(x),$ so $(x-2)$ divides $f(x)$ with zero remainder. To begin factoring $f(x),$ we can divide it by $(x-2)$ using synthetic division:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {x}^{3} & {x}^{2} & {x}^{1} & {x}^{0} \\\\ 2 & -1 & 3 & -3 & 2 \\\\  &  & -2 & 2 & -2 \\\\  & -1 & 1 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{f(x)}{x-2} & =-{x}^{2}+x-1 \\\\  & =-({x}^{2}-x+1),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\nf(x)=-(x-2)({x}^{2}-x+1).\n$$\n\nThe equation is now fully factored. Note that the discriminant of ${x}^{2}-x+1=0$ is \n\n$$\nD=(-1)^{2}-4(1)(1)=-3<0,\n$$\n\nwhich implies that the quadratic factor has no real roots. So by the zero-product rule, we deduce that $f(x)$ has a single root at $x=2.$ \n\nWe also find the $y$-intercept of the curve by substituting the value $x=0$ into the equation:\n\n$$\ny=-(0)^{3}+3(0)^{2}-3(0)+2=2\n$$\n\nSo, the curve:\n\n- has a $y$-intercept at $(0,2),$\n\n- passes through the $x$-axis at the single root $x=2,$ and\n\n- has no more $x$-intercepts.\n\nBecause the leading coefficient is negative, the graph has an $\\text{S}$-shape. Therefore, the graph looks as follows:\n\n![](images/f5/f542cc71eb968746be3ca9318c37751ec7486d2b15c002cfe85f3dbd956c4ebc.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c279a305-649b-54be-bddc-f2fbe9c77ed6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c279a305-649b-54be-bddc-f2fbe9c77ed6" :answer-field/id #uuid "c279a305-649b-54be-bddc-f2fbe9c77ed6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-06a46123-2c02-57fe-a199-738ca4a733b9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8b10f437-7656-5c74-9e12-be9baccb57d3" "answer-53660df8-84ef-5aa7-9892-f922f14a2c2b" "answer-fd9192da-41e0-536b-bd56-3a6ea641688a" "answer-06a46123-2c02-57fe-a199-738ca4a733b9" "answer-a9488348-cc11-5647-8684-1c7504f8a900"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8b10f437-7656-5c74-9e12-be9baccb57d3" :answer/id #uuid "8b10f437-7656-5c74-9e12-be9baccb57d3" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/41/419edd11da9b847f2d6d171624f5d25ca17131645f17a1cb652ceaac7ea4f115.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-53660df8-84ef-5aa7-9892-f922f14a2c2b" :answer/id #uuid "53660df8-84ef-5aa7-9892-f922f14a2c2b" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/76/763b0051c31d9ddada91b3a7ff34711fb055bbaf9897f385916a78d9518f89e7.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fd9192da-41e0-536b-bd56-3a6ea641688a" :answer/id #uuid "fd9192da-41e0-536b-bd56-3a6ea641688a" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/7e/7e4f0027cda5394a92678f06d27800bc99ff6ce0346293d3c23ad7f722245a98.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-06a46123-2c02-57fe-a199-738ca4a733b9" :answer/id #uuid "06a46123-2c02-57fe-a199-738ca4a733b9" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/f5/f542cc71eb968746be3ca9318c37751ec7486d2b15c002cfe85f3dbd956c4ebc.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a9488348-cc11-5647-8684-1c7504f8a900" :answer/id #uuid "a9488348-cc11-5647-8684-1c7504f8a900" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/f7/f773c005e94d94bcbfdf2d7a515711dea6d37449bfd8c8a59aa049c6775eb879.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162154 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-cb0efc72-9a29-58c3-a0f2-a7c2e7e96100"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-cb0efc72-9a29-58c3-a0f2-a7c2e7e96100" :question/id #uuid "cb0efc72-9a29-58c3-a0f2-a7c2e7e96100" :question/math-academy-id "q-143316" :question/problem "The marginal mass functions of the independent discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ are shown below. Given that the corresponding joint probability mass function is $f(x,y),$ find $f(4,3).$\n\n| | $x$ | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.7$ | |  | | $y$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.25$ | $0.6$ | $0.15$ | |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.7$ |\n| $y$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.25$ | $0.6$ | $0.15$ |" :question/worked-solution "Two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nTherefore, since our discrete random variables are independent, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(4,3) & ={f}_{X}(4)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(3) \\\\  & =0.2\\cdot 0.15 \\\\  & =0.03.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b6dc3fd8-a6ca-5e23-b3e1-64455b67f269"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b6dc3fd8-a6ca-5e23-b3e1-64455b67f269" :answer-field/id #uuid "b6dc3fd8-a6ca-5e23-b3e1-64455b67f269" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9bddfe86-7dc6-5540-86c3-4723fffc868b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cd3f228e-be2e-5c06-8182-1cd37eda6203" "answer-9bddfe86-7dc6-5540-86c3-4723fffc868b" "answer-bca06a6d-aa6b-587d-8442-4beee8f01b4b" "answer-256a3727-6321-59c1-b1c7-369f5a6a1518" "answer-a0426c68-78cb-5d58-9ffa-051f3b3cc1cc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cd3f228e-be2e-5c06-8182-1cd37eda6203" :answer/id #uuid "cd3f228e-be2e-5c06-8182-1cd37eda6203" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.025" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9bddfe86-7dc6-5540-86c3-4723fffc868b" :answer/id #uuid "9bddfe86-7dc6-5540-86c3-4723fffc868b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.03" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bca06a6d-aa6b-587d-8442-4beee8f01b4b" :answer/id #uuid "bca06a6d-aa6b-587d-8442-4beee8f01b4b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-256a3727-6321-59c1-b1c7-369f5a6a1518" :answer/id #uuid "256a3727-6321-59c1-b1c7-369f5a6a1518" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.175" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a0426c68-78cb-5d58-9ffa-051f3b3cc1cc" :answer/id #uuid "a0426c68-78cb-5d58-9ffa-051f3b3cc1cc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Impossible to determine using the given information." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162108 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8503a82e-cf30-5876-b2c2-50de2ef2f695"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-8503a82e-cf30-5876-b2c2-50de2ef2f695" :question/id #uuid "8503a82e-cf30-5876-b2c2-50de2ef2f695" :question/math-academy-id "q-143441" :question/problem "If ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a sample of size $n$ drawn from a population with mean $\\mu =4$ and variance ${\\sigma }^{2}=9,$  determine the smallest sample size required so that the standard error of the mean is less than $0.3.$" :question/worked-solution "If ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a sample of size $n$ from a population with population mean $\\mu $ and population variance ${\\sigma }^{2},$ then\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\mu ,\\,\\text{Var}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\frac{{\\sigma }^{2}}{n},\n$$\n\nand the standard error is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{SE}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[\\overset{―}{X}]}=\\frac{\\sigma }{\\sqrt{n}}\n$$\n\nSince the population standard deviation is $\\sigma =\\sqrt{9}=3,$ we have that \n\n$$\n\\text{SE}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{n}}.\n$$\n\nWe require that the standard error is less than $0.3.$ Therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{n}} & <0.3 \\\\ \\sqrt{n} & >\\frac{3}{0.3} \\\\ \\sqrt{n} & >10 \\\\ n & >{10}^{2} \\\\ n & >100.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest sample size is $n=101.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9c59848f-dfee-5b4c-8761-3808942e6743"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9c59848f-dfee-5b4c-8761-3808942e6743" :answer-field/id #uuid "9c59848f-dfee-5b4c-8761-3808942e6743" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e069f6a1-671b-5f98-9ba7-f48db9f9cb74" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e069f6a1-671b-5f98-9ba7-f48db9f9cb74" "answer-8b54b2bf-266b-54ff-a5d4-a1ac6399e630" "answer-7fa3c38a-049e-59c3-a98c-3e5dbd6f1ba8" "answer-dd64b03b-72a4-5d77-bbef-f658fdcb9c0e" "answer-a3fe3947-9796-56a3-9f64-a73a496fe76c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e069f6a1-671b-5f98-9ba7-f48db9f9cb74" :answer/id #uuid "e069f6a1-671b-5f98-9ba7-f48db9f9cb74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "101" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8b54b2bf-266b-54ff-a5d4-a1ac6399e630" :answer/id #uuid "8b54b2bf-266b-54ff-a5d4-a1ac6399e630" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7fa3c38a-049e-59c3-a98c-3e5dbd6f1ba8" :answer/id #uuid "7fa3c38a-049e-59c3-a98c-3e5dbd6f1ba8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dd64b03b-72a4-5d77-bbef-f658fdcb9c0e" :answer/id #uuid "dd64b03b-72a4-5d77-bbef-f658fdcb9c0e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "178" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a3fe3947-9796-56a3-9f64-a73a496fe76c" :answer/id #uuid "a3fe3947-9796-56a3-9f64-a73a496fe76c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1\\,001" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186176063 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-bc219d25-3086-59ef-9782-ded17eb3bf3e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-bc219d25-3086-59ef-9782-ded17eb3bf3e" :question/id #uuid "bc219d25-3086-59ef-9782-ded17eb3bf3e" :question/math-academy-id "q-159828" :question/problem "Suppose ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{5}$ is an I.I.D random sample with ${X}_{i}∼Po(\\theta )$ and unknown rate parameter $\\theta .$ For a particular sample ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{5},$ you're given that \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{x}_{i}=6,\\,{\\prod }_{i=1}^{5}({x}_{i})!=2.\n$$\n\nFind the likelihood function of the sample.\n\n*Hint: The probability mass function for a Poisson distribution is given by* \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{\\theta }^{x}{e}^{-\\theta }}{x!},\\,x=0,1,2,…\n$$\n\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ are independent and identically distributed discrete random variables with probability mass function $f(x;\\theta ),$ where $\\theta $ is an unknown parameter, then the likelihood function of a random sample ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ is\n\n$$\nL(\\theta )={\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i};\\theta ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we are given a sample of $n=5$ independent Poisson random variables with unknown parameter $\\theta ,$ for which the probability mass function is\n\n$$\nf(x;\\theta )=\\frac{{\\theta }^{x}{e}^{-\\theta }}{x!},\\,x=0,1,2,…\\,.\n$$\n\nWe can calculate the likelihood function as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(\\theta ) & ={\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i};\\theta ) \\\\  & ={\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}\\frac{{\\theta }^{{x}_{i}}{e}^{-\\theta }}{{x}_{i}!} \\\\  & =(\\frac{{\\theta }^{{x}_{1}}{e}^{-\\theta }}{{x}_{1}!})\\cdot (\\frac{{\\theta }^{{x}_{2}}{e}^{-\\theta }}{{x}_{2}!})⋯(\\frac{{\\theta }^{{x}_{n}}{e}^{-\\theta }}{{x}_{n}!}) \\\\  & ={\\theta }^{\\sum {x}_{i}}\\cdot {e}^{-\\sum \\theta }\\cdot {\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}\\frac{1}{({x}_{i})!} \\\\  & ={\\theta }^{\\sum {x}_{i}}\\cdot {e}^{-n\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{1}{{\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i})!} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{C}\\,{\\theta }^{S}\\,{e}^{-n\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C={\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i})!$ is a constant and $S={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}.$\n\nWe are told that $S={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}=6,$ $C={\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i})!=2,$ and $n=5.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(\\theta ) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,{\\theta }^{6}\\,{e}^{-5\\theta }.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ad515c88-9b38-55db-8768-e6ecd6bc622d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ad515c88-9b38-55db-8768-e6ecd6bc622d" :answer-field/id #uuid "ad515c88-9b38-55db-8768-e6ecd6bc622d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-cc522095-22b1-5624-b7a0-a0812f90bbaa" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a96ab3af-cd62-5678-ac9c-8c6618db455f" "answer-6a57da15-ddaa-5736-9607-b78903457fec" "answer-dce7f679-1acd-5a35-a482-1d3a87996165" "answer-cc522095-22b1-5624-b7a0-a0812f90bbaa" "answer-647c8191-dcba-53e2-a8ed-6c6a3acc2dd5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a96ab3af-cd62-5678-ac9c-8c6618db455f" :answer/id #uuid "a96ab3af-cd62-5678-ac9c-8c6618db455f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,{\\theta }^{6}\\,{e}^{-2\\theta }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6a57da15-ddaa-5736-9607-b78903457fec" :answer/id #uuid "6a57da15-ddaa-5736-9607-b78903457fec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\,{\\theta }^{5}\\,{e}^{-6\\theta }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dce7f679-1acd-5a35-a482-1d3a87996165" :answer/id #uuid "dce7f679-1acd-5a35-a482-1d3a87996165" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\,{\\theta }^{2}\\,{e}^{-5\\theta }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cc522095-22b1-5624-b7a0-a0812f90bbaa" :answer/id #uuid "cc522095-22b1-5624-b7a0-a0812f90bbaa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\,{\\theta }^{6}\\,{e}^{-5\\theta }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-647c8191-dcba-53e2-a8ed-6c6a3acc2dd5" :answer/id #uuid "647c8191-dcba-53e2-a8ed-6c6a3acc2dd5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}\\,{\\theta }^{2}\\,{e}^{-6\\theta }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162095 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-903f2879-32c5-5f80-9994-a71eea52244c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-903f2879-32c5-5f80-9994-a71eea52244c" :question/id #uuid "903f2879-32c5-5f80-9994-a71eea52244c" :question/math-academy-id "q-138637" :question/problem "$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the observation matrix $X$ above, where the individual observations are given in columns. Find the sample covariance matrix of the data." :question/worked-solution "Recall that  the sample covariance matrix is given by\n\n$$\nC=\\frac{1}{n-1}B{B}^{T},\n$$\n\nwhere $B$ is the observation matrix in the mean-deviation form, and $n$ is the number of observations.\n\nSo, we first need to compute the mean-deviation form of our observation matrix.\n\nThe sample mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{1}{3}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}([\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} & ={x}_{1}-m=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {b}_{2} & ={x}_{2}-m=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {b}_{3} & ={x}_{3}-m=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  the mean-deviation form is\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, the sample covariance matrix is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =\\frac{1}{3-1}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f0fcff68-ef82-5cf2-80e9-66e229051d3b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f0fcff68-ef82-5cf2-80e9-66e229051d3b" :answer-field/id #uuid "f0fcff68-ef82-5cf2-80e9-66e229051d3b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ab0dabcb-1994-53de-9ca9-1943be5e5cde" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ab0dabcb-1994-53de-9ca9-1943be5e5cde" "answer-af3ec0f0-e34b-503b-876e-317e6bdbb214" "answer-32553198-4247-5c51-aaff-735cd1f400b3" "answer-5089ccec-dbdc-5176-876d-be7464e512d0" "answer-9d1835d4-2d7a-5203-af02-da60f52fa656"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ab0dabcb-1994-53de-9ca9-1943be5e5cde" :answer/id #uuid "ab0dabcb-1994-53de-9ca9-1943be5e5cde" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-af3ec0f0-e34b-503b-876e-317e6bdbb214" :answer/id #uuid "af3ec0f0-e34b-503b-876e-317e6bdbb214" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-32553198-4247-5c51-aaff-735cd1f400b3" :answer/id #uuid "32553198-4247-5c51-aaff-735cd1f400b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5089ccec-dbdc-5176-876d-be7464e512d0" :answer/id #uuid "5089ccec-dbdc-5176-876d-be7464e512d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9d1835d4-2d7a-5203-af02-da60f52fa656" :answer/id #uuid "9d1835d4-2d7a-5203-af02-da60f52fa656" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186115317 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ad031c31-3240-524a-8691-42d16ca618b6"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-ad031c31-3240-524a-8691-42d16ca618b6" :question/id #uuid "ad031c31-3240-524a-8691-42d16ca618b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-95813" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X∼B(200,0.4),$ use the normal approximation to the binomial distribution to approximate $P(X>90).$ Give your final answer to three decimal places.\n\n*Hint: The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,1.4\\,$ | $\\,0.9192\\,$ | $\\,0.9207\\,$ | $\\,0.9222\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.5\\,$ | $\\,0.9332\\,$ | $\\,0.9345\\,$ | $\\,0.9357\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.6\\,$ | $\\,0.9452\\,$ | $\\,0.9463\\,$ | $\\,0.9474\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "Given a binomial random variable $X∼B(n,p),$ if \n\n- $np>5,$ and\n\n- $n(1-p)>5,$\n\nwe can approximate $X$ as a normal random variable $Y$ with mean $\\mu =np$ and variance ${\\sigma }^{2}=np(1-p),$ that is, \n\n$$\nY∼N(np,np(1-p)).\n$$\n\nHere, we have $n=200$ and $p=0.4.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}np & =200\\cdot 0.4 \\\\  & =80 \\\\  & >5\\,✓ \\\\ n(1-p) & =200\\cdot (1-0.4) \\\\  & =120 \\\\  & >5.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can approximate our binomial random variable $X$ with a normal random variable $Y$ with mean\n\n$$\n\\mu =np=(200)(0.4)=80\n$$\n\nand variance\n\n$$\n{\\sigma }^{2}=np(1-p)=(200)(0.4)(1-0.4)=48.\n$$\n\nThat is, we can approximate $X$ by $Y∼N(80,48).$\n\nNow, we can estimate the desired probability $P(X>90).$ Using a continuity correction, we have\n\n$$\nP(X>90)=P(X\\ge 91)≈P(Y>90.5).\n$$\n\nTo compute this probability, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y>90.5) & =P(Z>\\frac{90.5-80}{\\sqrt{48}}) \\\\  & ≈P(Z>1.52) \\\\  & =1-P(Z\\le 1.52) \\\\  & =1-Φ(1.52) \\\\  & =1-0.9357 \\\\  & =0.0643\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(X>90)≈0.064.\n$$\n\nNote: Using a software package for the approximation gives a probability of $0.0648.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9888a54d-c871-5c1f-82d5-84bd3b3a9c80"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9888a54d-c871-5c1f-82d5-84bd3b3a9c80" :answer-field/id #uuid "9888a54d-c871-5c1f-82d5-84bd3b3a9c80" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c5499a75-3f11-5a8b-beb6-47826166db4a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3dff2c88-1c0e-5737-a541-f914177727d0" "answer-66435b11-79f7-56d4-9d25-f13c155dd3fe" "answer-c5499a75-3f11-5a8b-beb6-47826166db4a" "answer-c939d6f5-8f5a-5c19-8227-a4af12e4d421" "answer-2d626ef2-fe19-5615-864f-93b3f020facc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3dff2c88-1c0e-5737-a541-f914177727d0" :answer/id #uuid "3dff2c88-1c0e-5737-a541-f914177727d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.048" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-66435b11-79f7-56d4-9d25-f13c155dd3fe" :answer/id #uuid "66435b11-79f7-56d4-9d25-f13c155dd3fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.055" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c5499a75-3f11-5a8b-beb6-47826166db4a" :answer/id #uuid "c5499a75-3f11-5a8b-beb6-47826166db4a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.064" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c939d6f5-8f5a-5c19-8227-a4af12e4d421" :answer/id #uuid "c939d6f5-8f5a-5c19-8227-a4af12e4d421" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.072" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2d626ef2-fe19-5615-864f-93b3f020facc" :answer/id #uuid "2d626ef2-fe19-5615-864f-93b3f020facc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.091" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186176042 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-803f66d6-b1cb-5f24-9bcd-afd86a0fb084"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-803f66d6-b1cb-5f24-9bcd-afd86a0fb084" :question/id #uuid "803f66d6-b1cb-5f24-9bcd-afd86a0fb084" :question/math-academy-id "q-143802" :question/problem "A random variable $X$ has the probability distribution given below.\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}, & x=0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}, & x=1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}, & x=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[{X}^{3}].$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ is a discrete random variable with probability mass function $f(x)$ and sample space $S,$ the expected value of ${X}^{3}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{3}]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}{x}^{3}\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each cubed value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{3}] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in S}{x}^{3}\\cdot f(x) \\\\  & ={0}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}+{1}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}+{2}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =0\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}+1\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}+8\\cdot \\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =0+\\frac{1}{4}+2 \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b124b7e8-f665-5416-a587-c5c709c95b52"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b124b7e8-f665-5416-a587-c5c709c95b52" :answer-field/id #uuid "b124b7e8-f665-5416-a587-c5c709c95b52" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-05d0bed3-2f44-5147-8b11-1799b1a77a53" :answer-field/choices ["answer-164c9de6-1afb-5748-ad52-794c0b12deda" "answer-2ed70e6b-a2cd-51da-96fd-f5a213dd7fd1" "answer-cb9f5533-060f-5f5e-99fa-71a91f1849d0" "answer-7db5c39d-db73-5155-8d2f-1ed953fb569c" "answer-05d0bed3-2f44-5147-8b11-1799b1a77a53"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-164c9de6-1afb-5748-ad52-794c0b12deda" :answer/id #uuid "164c9de6-1afb-5748-ad52-794c0b12deda" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2ed70e6b-a2cd-51da-96fd-f5a213dd7fd1" :answer/id #uuid "2ed70e6b-a2cd-51da-96fd-f5a213dd7fd1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{13}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cb9f5533-060f-5f5e-99fa-71a91f1849d0" :answer/id #uuid "cb9f5533-060f-5f5e-99fa-71a91f1849d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7db5c39d-db73-5155-8d2f-1ed953fb569c" :answer/id #uuid "7db5c39d-db73-5155-8d2f-1ed953fb569c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-05d0bed3-2f44-5147-8b11-1799b1a77a53" :answer/id #uuid "05d0bed3-2f44-5147-8b11-1799b1a77a53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186234235 :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9596f751-f676-5a62-bf63-b8794255c731"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9596f751-f676-5a62-bf63-b8794255c731" :answer-field/id #uuid "9596f751-f676-5a62-bf63-b8794255c731" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1fe24ca2-15a6-51f1-a1df-7cc11fbacd48" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2cd556ca-30b4-5288-8d72-abfec4b7f03d" "answer-a1d45a8f-d17e-5c84-8b87-5a64a5a6e762" "answer-1fe24ca2-15a6-51f1-a1df-7cc11fbacd48" "answer-debab0a7-4e2a-5e76-9d88-682a5f66970d" "answer-4ef2bdba-9ddd-528c-9cea-425b4e82d718"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2cd556ca-30b4-5288-8d72-abfec4b7f03d" :answer/id #uuid "2cd556ca-30b4-5288-8d72-abfec4b7f03d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a1d45a8f-d17e-5c84-8b87-5a64a5a6e762" :answer/id #uuid "a1d45a8f-d17e-5c84-8b87-5a64a5a6e762" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1fe24ca2-15a6-51f1-a1df-7cc11fbacd48" :answer/id #uuid "1fe24ca2-15a6-51f1-a1df-7cc11fbacd48" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-debab0a7-4e2a-5e76-9d88-682a5f66970d" :answer/id #uuid "debab0a7-4e2a-5e76-9d88-682a5f66970d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4ef2bdba-9ddd-528c-9cea-425b4e82d718" :answer/id #uuid "4ef2bdba-9ddd-528c-9cea-425b4e82d718" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186120471 :question/problem "Which of the three sequences below are geometric sequences?\n\n- $5,\\,10,\\,15,\\,…$\n- ${a}_{n+1}=6{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=18,\\,n\\ge 1$\n- $f(n+1)=2f(n)+3,\\,f(1)=1,\\,n\\ge 1$" :question/worked-solution "A sequence is geometric if there is a common ratio between its terms. Let's check each sequence in turn.\n\n- Sequence I is not geometric because not every pair of consecutive terms has the same ratio. To see this, we only need to go up to the third term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{f(2)}{f(1)}=\\frac{10}{5} & =2 \\\\ \\frac{f(3)}{f(2)}=\\frac{15}{10} & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Sequence II is a geometric sequence. The recursive rule ${a}_{n+1}=6{a}_{n}$ tells us that each term is $6$ times the previous term, so the common ratio is $r=6.$\n\n- Sequence III is not a geometric sequence. To see this, we can calculate the first $3$ terms of the sequence and then compute the ratios of consecutive terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1) & =1 \\\\ f(2) & =2\\cdot 1+3=5 \\\\ f(3) & =2\\cdot 5+3=13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the first two pairs of consecutive terms have different ratios:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{f(2)}{f(1)}=\\frac{5}{1} & =5 \\\\ \\frac{f(3)}{f(2)}=\\frac{13}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, only sequence II is a geometric sequence." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f414d04e-db2f-5c79-9901-f372e116f217"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f414d04e-db2f-5c79-9901-f372e116f217" :answer-field/id #uuid "f414d04e-db2f-5c79-9901-f372e116f217" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a0b748f5-2a5a-58b1-8b00-e4539a016a0d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-268dacd3-22a7-5029-a61f-0917d072e1d0" "answer-d78f3139-3e6e-5fcf-ac06-14a236d3600d" "answer-adf88bc5-89c1-54d7-bbbe-75f580ceecd1" "answer-a0b748f5-2a5a-58b1-8b00-e4539a016a0d" "answer-ee3f0955-7c16-5a2f-810b-5ade22ecf32d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-268dacd3-22a7-5029-a61f-0917d072e1d0" :answer/id #uuid "268dacd3-22a7-5029-a61f-0917d072e1d0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d78f3139-3e6e-5fcf-ac06-14a236d3600d" :answer/id #uuid "d78f3139-3e6e-5fcf-ac06-14a236d3600d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-adf88bc5-89c1-54d7-bbbe-75f580ceecd1" :answer/id #uuid "adf88bc5-89c1-54d7-bbbe-75f580ceecd1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a0b748f5-2a5a-58b1-8b00-e4539a016a0d" :answer/id #uuid "a0b748f5-2a5a-58b1-8b00-e4539a016a0d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ee3f0955-7c16-5a2f-810b-5ade22ecf32d" :answer/id #uuid "ee3f0955-7c16-5a2f-810b-5ade22ecf32d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105819 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-296758d7-4a30-5e40-8387-2f49e4f79d97"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-296758d7-4a30-5e40-8387-2f49e4f79d97" :question/id #uuid "296758d7-4a30-5e40-8387-2f49e4f79d97" :question/math-academy-id "q-83780" :question/problem "| $y$ | $1$ | $4$ | $9$ | $16$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(Y=y)$ | $0.4$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ | $0.1$ |\n\nCompute $P(Y<10)$ given that the random variable $Y$ has the probability mass function shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y<10) & =P(y\\in {1,4,9}) \\\\  & =P(Y=1)+P(Y=4)+P(Y=9) \\\\  & =0.4+0.2+0.3 \\\\  & =0.9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0961bf99-126c-5534-ba16-bea193b90bf3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0961bf99-126c-5534-ba16-bea193b90bf3" :answer-field/id #uuid "0961bf99-126c-5534-ba16-bea193b90bf3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-76e050ef-9ea6-57db-a93e-738c9ce0e484" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4e63bc87-94c1-5b9a-985b-f10b2beaa419" "answer-ed3473ab-309f-5376-bfac-a14554d35c2c" "answer-104ab4a2-7106-52c9-b66c-648885f6526d" "answer-76e050ef-9ea6-57db-a93e-738c9ce0e484" "answer-b7be7c9d-4987-5dd6-95f7-5a48cc725e3c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4e63bc87-94c1-5b9a-985b-f10b2beaa419" :answer/id #uuid "4e63bc87-94c1-5b9a-985b-f10b2beaa419" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ed3473ab-309f-5376-bfac-a14554d35c2c" :answer/id #uuid "ed3473ab-309f-5376-bfac-a14554d35c2c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-104ab4a2-7106-52c9-b66c-648885f6526d" :answer/id #uuid "104ab4a2-7106-52c9-b66c-648885f6526d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-76e050ef-9ea6-57db-a93e-738c9ce0e484" :answer/id #uuid "76e050ef-9ea6-57db-a93e-738c9ce0e484" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b7be7c9d-4987-5dd6-95f7-5a48cc725e3c" :answer/id #uuid "b7be7c9d-4987-5dd6-95f7-5a48cc725e3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186078563 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-9740bcef-2a83-552d-9db0-632ce64e6011"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-9740bcef-2a83-552d-9db0-632ce64e6011" :question/id #uuid "9740bcef-2a83-552d-9db0-632ce64e6011" :question/math-academy-id "q-77886" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{\\sqrt{a}-\\sqrt{b}}{4\\sqrt{b}}\\,$ without radicals in the denominator." :question/worked-solution "To remove the radical $\\sqrt{b}$ from the denominator, we multiply both the numerator and denominator by $\\sqrt{b}$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{a}-\\sqrt{b}}{4\\sqrt{b}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{a}-\\sqrt{b}}{4\\sqrt{b}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{b}}{\\sqrt{b}} & = \\\\ \\frac{(\\sqrt{a}-\\sqrt{b})\\sqrt{b}}{4(\\sqrt{b})^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{a}\\cdot \\sqrt{b}-(\\sqrt{b})^{2}}{4(\\sqrt{b})^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{ab}-b}{4b}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-66448a61-1f26-5e7e-a756-7e6120ce1b93"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-66448a61-1f26-5e7e-a756-7e6120ce1b93" :answer-field/id #uuid "66448a61-1f26-5e7e-a756-7e6120ce1b93" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-aa82d8aa-f13b-58b4-bb31-9edaa9f0fdd3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bfacf6f8-3a02-5c30-9cd8-59f545117ccc" "answer-aa82d8aa-f13b-58b4-bb31-9edaa9f0fdd3" "answer-4a67fe05-eddb-551c-bfbb-b46c0a2ba0f3" "answer-9575bbba-541f-5939-ab74-aaab428aa24b" "answer-47d8d125-9abc-5899-89d9-d8880316794d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bfacf6f8-3a02-5c30-9cd8-59f545117ccc" :answer/id #uuid "bfacf6f8-3a02-5c30-9cd8-59f545117ccc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{ab}-1}{4b}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aa82d8aa-f13b-58b4-bb31-9edaa9f0fdd3" :answer/id #uuid "aa82d8aa-f13b-58b4-bb31-9edaa9f0fdd3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{ab}-b}{4b}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4a67fe05-eddb-551c-bfbb-b46c0a2ba0f3" :answer/id #uuid "4a67fe05-eddb-551c-bfbb-b46c0a2ba0f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{a}-1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9575bbba-541f-5939-ab74-aaab428aa24b" :answer/id #uuid "9575bbba-541f-5939-ab74-aaab428aa24b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{a}-\\sqrt{b}}{4b}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-47d8d125-9abc-5899-89d9-d8880316794d" :answer/id #uuid "47d8d125-9abc-5899-89d9-d8880316794d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{b}-a}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186115219 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b6488fce-f74c-5334-a4ac-d8d71ef00e69"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-b6488fce-f74c-5334-a4ac-d8d71ef00e69" :question/id #uuid "b6488fce-f74c-5334-a4ac-d8d71ef00e69" :question/math-academy-id "q-3090" :question/problem "Solve for $n$ where ${16}^{2n}={8}^{n+1}.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this equation, we need both exponential terms to have a common base. To do this, we rewrite the equation using $16={2}^{4}$ and $8={2}^{3},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{({2}^{4})}^{2n}={({2}^{3})}^{n+1}\\,\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the power rule of exponents. This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{2}^{8n} & ={2}^{3(n+1)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since both sides of the equation share the same base $(2)$, we equate the exponents and solve for $n:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8n & =3(n+1) \\\\ 8n & =3n+3 \\\\ 5n & =3 \\\\ n & =\\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2c131e70-66d3-5684-931b-600e5433ed9b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2c131e70-66d3-5684-931b-600e5433ed9b" :answer-field/id #uuid "2c131e70-66d3-5684-931b-600e5433ed9b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c45e66f0-50f2-598c-b5d0-5402c3cbc44b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2ebed13b-65b6-5f09-b6ac-5843bb401594" "answer-e52fbbd7-076f-5ca8-a202-557210987158" "answer-8a7cd739-dad9-5004-a078-dfdfdfb9ad48" "answer-c45e66f0-50f2-598c-b5d0-5402c3cbc44b" "answer-083bbb43-125e-530a-a0bf-4e386e0fef8e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2ebed13b-65b6-5f09-b6ac-5843bb401594" :answer/id #uuid "2ebed13b-65b6-5f09-b6ac-5843bb401594" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e52fbbd7-076f-5ca8-a202-557210987158" :answer/id #uuid "e52fbbd7-076f-5ca8-a202-557210987158" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8a7cd739-dad9-5004-a078-dfdfdfb9ad48" :answer/id #uuid "8a7cd739-dad9-5004-a078-dfdfdfb9ad48" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c45e66f0-50f2-598c-b5d0-5402c3cbc44b" :answer/id #uuid "c45e66f0-50f2-598c-b5d0-5402c3cbc44b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-083bbb43-125e-530a-a0bf-4e386e0fef8e" :answer/id #uuid "083bbb43-125e-530a-a0bf-4e386e0fef8e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054759 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-809412f4-737f-5a7f-aa0e-0c96aef026e3"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-809412f4-737f-5a7f-aa0e-0c96aef026e3" :question/id #uuid "809412f4-737f-5a7f-aa0e-0c96aef026e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-293739" :question/problem "Rationalize the denominator of $\\frac{1+\\sqrt{6}}{\\sqrt{10}-\\sqrt{3}}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that the denominator's conjugate is $\\sqrt{10}+\\sqrt{3}.$\n\nNow, to rationalize the denominator, we multiply both the numerator and denominator by the conjugate $\\sqrt{10}+\\sqrt{3},$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1+\\sqrt{6}}{\\sqrt{10}-\\sqrt{3}} & = \\\\ \\frac{1+\\sqrt{6}}{\\sqrt{10}-\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{10}+\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{10}+\\sqrt{3}} & = \\\\ \\frac{(1+\\sqrt{6})(\\sqrt{1}0+\\sqrt{3})}{(\\sqrt{10}-\\sqrt{3})(\\sqrt{1}0+\\sqrt{3})} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{10}+\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{60}+\\sqrt{18}}{(\\sqrt{10})^{2}-(\\sqrt{3})^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{10}+\\sqrt{3}+2\\sqrt{15}+3\\sqrt{2}}{10-3} & = \\\\ \\frac{3\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{10}+2\\sqrt{15}}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c2ea22de-638e-5104-ae1a-904032c8e659"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c2ea22de-638e-5104-ae1a-904032c8e659" :answer-field/id #uuid "c2ea22de-638e-5104-ae1a-904032c8e659" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f2b527ba-9c52-5c95-9e0f-cd91704806e4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-482654bc-a522-5c5c-8a44-d4ee24bd95bf" "answer-f2b527ba-9c52-5c95-9e0f-cd91704806e4" "answer-4b94d91c-f649-53fe-abf1-ed4fae112291" "answer-6c5459bc-05a6-570e-8c22-2d312daed4ba" "answer-7b9e2051-9eec-5423-bfe6-d13f30f71ad4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-482654bc-a522-5c5c-8a44-d4ee24bd95bf" :answer/id #uuid "482654bc-a522-5c5c-8a44-d4ee24bd95bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{10}+\\sqrt{3}+2\\sqrt{15}+3\\sqrt{2}}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {: